{
  "meta": {
    "id": "apstats-u6-inference-prop",
    "name": "Inference for Proportions (6.1-6.2)",
    "subject": "AP Statistics",
    "description": "Logic of significance testing, confidence intervals for a population proportion: identify procedures, check conditions, calculate standard error, critical values, margin of error, confidence intervals, and minimum sample size"
  },
  "config": {
    "contextsFile": null,
    "skills": [
      "VAR-1.H",
      "UNC-4.A",
      "UNC-4.B",
      "UNC-4.C",
      "UNC-4.D",
      "UNC-4.E"
    ]
  },
  "display": {
    "showGraph": false,
    "graphType": null,
    "infoPanel": [
      {
        "label": "Topic",
        "value": "{{topicId}}"
      },
      {
        "label": "Scenario",
        "value": "{{scenarioText}}"
      },
      {
        "label": "Given",
        "value": "{{givenText}}"
      }
    ]
  },
  "modes": [
    {
      "id": "l01-identify-evidence",
      "name": "6.1a: Identify Evidence",
      "animation": "assets/IdentifyEvidence.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": "default",
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "evidenceAnswer",
            "type": "choice",
            "label": "{{questionText}}",
            "options": [
              "{{optA}}",
              "{{optB}}"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l02-two-explanations",
      "name": "6.1b: Two Explanations",
      "animation": "assets/TwoExplanations.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "explanationAnswer",
            "type": "dropdown",
            "label": "Which correctly describes the two possible explanations for the study result?",
            "options": [
              "{{optA}}",
              "{{optB}}",
              "{{optC}}",
              "{{optD}}"
            ],
            "placeholder": "Choose..."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l03-convincing-evidence",
      "name": "6.1c: Is Evidence Convincing?",
      "animation": "assets/ConvincingEvidence.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "convincingAnswer",
            "type": "choice",
            "label": "Do the data provide convincing evidence for the claim?",
            "options": [
              "Yes, convincing evidence",
              "No, not convincing evidence"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "convincingExplain",
            "type": "textarea",
            "label": "Explain your reasoning:",
            "rows": 3,
            "placeholder": "Reference the simulation probability..."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l04-identify-procedure",
      "name": "6.2a: Identify the Procedure",
      "animation": "assets/IdentifyProcedure.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "procedureAnswer",
            "type": "dropdown",
            "label": "What inference procedure should be used?",
            "options": [
              "{{optA}}",
              "{{optB}}",
              "{{optC}}",
              "{{optD}}"
            ],
            "placeholder": "Choose..."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l05-check-conditions",
      "name": "6.2b: Check Conditions",
      "animation": "assets/CheckConditions.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "conditionsMet",
            "type": "choice",
            "label": "Are ALL conditions for inference met?",
            "options": [
              "Yes, all conditions are met",
              "No, at least one condition fails"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "conditionsExplain",
            "type": "textarea",
            "label": "Explain which conditions are met or not met:",
            "rows": 3,
            "placeholder": "Check: random, 10%, large counts..."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l06-standard-error",
      "name": "6.2c: Standard Error",
      "animation": "assets/StandardError.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "seAnswer",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Calculate SE(p\u0302) = \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n). Round to 4 decimal places:",
            "step": 0.0001,
            "min": 0
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l07-critical-value",
      "name": "6.2d: Critical Values",
      "animation": "assets/CriticalValues.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "zStarAnswer",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "What is the critical value z* for a {{confLevel}}% confidence interval?",
            "step": 0.001
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l08-margin-of-error",
      "name": "6.2e: Margin of Error",
      "animation": "assets/MarginOfError.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "meAnswer",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Calculate the margin of error (z* \u00d7 SE). Round to 4 decimal places:",
            "step": 0.0001,
            "min": 0
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l09-confidence-interval",
      "name": "6.2f: Calculate the CI",
      "animation": "assets/ConfidenceInterval.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "ciLower",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Lower bound of the confidence interval:",
            "step": 0.001
          },
          {
            "id": "ciUpper",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Upper bound of the confidence interval:",
            "step": 0.001
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l10-min-sample-size",
      "name": "6.2g: Minimum Sample Size",
      "animation": "assets/MinSampleSize.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 1
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "sampleSizeAnswer",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "What is the minimum sample size needed? (Round UP to nearest integer)",
            "step": 1,
            "min": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l11-capstone-62",
      "name": "6.2 Capstone",
      "animation": "assets/CapstoneSynthesis.mp4",
      "unlockedBy": {
        "gold": 3
      },
      "layout": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "capstoneConditions",
            "type": "choice",
            "label": "Are all conditions for inference met?",
            "options": [
              "Yes, all conditions are met",
              "No, at least one condition fails"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "capstoneLower",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Lower bound of the CI:",
            "step": 0.001
          },
          {
            "id": "capstoneUpper",
            "type": "number",
            "label": "Upper bound of the CI:",
            "step": 0.001
          },
          {
            "id": "capstoneExplain",
            "type": "textarea",
            "label": "Interpret the confidence interval in context:",
            "rows": 3,
            "placeholder": "We are __% confident that..."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "grading": {
    "rubricFile": "grading-rules.js",
    "aiPromptFile": "ai-grader-prompt.txt",
    "scoring": {
      "scale": ["E", "P", "I"],
      "meanings": {
        "E": "Essentially Correct",
        "P": "Partially Correct",
        "I": "Incorrect"
      }
    }
  },
  "hints": {
    "perField": {
      "evidenceAnswer": "Evidence = how the sample result (p\u0302) compares to the expected value. Is p\u0302 above or below what we'd expect if the claim were false?",
      "explanationAnswer": "There are always exactly two explanations: (1) the result happened by CHANCE alone, or (2) there is a REAL effect.",
      "convincingAnswer": "If the probability of getting the result by chance alone is small (roughly less than 5%), the evidence IS convincing.",
      "convincingExplain": "Reference the simulation: 'Because ___ out of ___ simulations produced results this extreme, it is [likely/unlikely] to happen by chance alone.'",
      "procedureAnswer": "Ask: How many samples? (one) What data type? (proportion) What's the goal? (estimate with CI) \u2192 One-sample z-interval for p.",
      "conditionsMet": "Three conditions: (1) Random sample, (2) n \u2264 10% of N, (3) np\u0302 \u2265 10 AND n(1\u2212p\u0302) \u2265 10. ALL must be met.",
      "conditionsExplain": "Show the numbers for each: Random? \u2713/\u2717. 10%: n = ___ \u2264 10% of N = ___? Large counts: np\u0302 = ___ \u2265 10? n(1\u2212p\u0302) = ___ \u2265 10?",
      "seAnswer": "SE(p\u0302) = \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n). Plug in the sample proportion and sample size.",
      "zStarAnswer": "Common z* values: 90% \u2192 1.645, 95% \u2192 1.960, 99% \u2192 2.576.",
      "meAnswer": "Margin of error = z* \u00d7 SE(p\u0302). Multiply the critical value by the standard error.",
      "ciLower": "Lower bound = p\u0302 \u2212 (margin of error) = p\u0302 \u2212 z* \u00d7 \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n)",
      "ciUpper": "Upper bound = p\u0302 + (margin of error) = p\u0302 + z* \u00d7 \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n)",
      "sampleSizeAnswer": "Solve: n \u2265 p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302) \u00d7 (z*/ME)\u00b2. Use p\u0302 = 0.5 if no prior estimate. Always round UP!",
      "capstoneConditions": "Check: (1) Random? (2) n \u2264 10% of N? (3) Both np\u0302 \u2265 10 and n(1\u2212p\u0302) \u2265 10?",
      "capstoneLower": "Lower bound = p\u0302 \u2212 z* \u00d7 \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n)",
      "capstoneUpper": "Upper bound = p\u0302 + z* \u00d7 \u221a(p\u0302(1\u2212p\u0302)/n)",
      "capstoneExplain": "Template: 'We are __% confident that the interval from ___ to ___ captures the true proportion of [context].'"
    },
    "penalty": {
      "0": "gold",
      "1": "silver",
      "2": "bronze",
      "3": "tin"
    }
  },
